Subject: kmemleak-add-the-base-support-fix
From: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>

prio_tree_init() can be run even earlier, so we may as well do so.

Cc: Catalin Marinas <catalin.marinas@arm.com>
Cc: Ingo Molnar <mingo@elte.hu>
Cc: Paul E. McKenney <paulmck@linux.vnet.ibm.com>
Cc: Pekka Enberg <penberg@cs.helsinki.fi>
Signed-off-by: Andrew Morton <akpm@linux-foundation.org>
---

 init/main.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff -puN init/main.c~kmemleak-add-the-base-support-fix init/main.c
--- a/init/main.c~kmemleak-add-the-base-support-fix
+++ a/init/main.c
@@ -669,6 +669,7 @@ asmlinkage void __init start_kernel(void
 		initrd_start = 0;
 	}
 #endif
+	prio_tree_init();
 	vmalloc_init();
 	vfs_caches_init_early();
 	cpuset_init_early();
@@ -677,7 +678,6 @@ asmlinkage void __init start_kernel(void
 	enable_debug_pagealloc();
 	cpu_hotplug_init();
 	kmem_cache_init();
-	prio_tree_init();
 	kmemleak_init();
 	kmemtrace_init();
 	debug_objects_mem_init();
_

